d.I("A \"most stable partner\" is therefore evidence only if it is specific to the passage and survives the removal of its strongest word. The scan also fails silently on μεθίστημι (\"transfer\"), on the aorists and futures of ῥύομαι (\"rescue\"), on oblique φῶς (\"light\") and on δέω (\"bind\") `[S: audit 4]`.","A \"most stable partner\" is therefore evidence only if it is specific to the passage and survives the removal of its strongest word. The scan also fails silently on μεθίστημι (\"transfer\"), on the aorists and futures of ῥύομαι (\"rescue\"), on oblique φῶς (\"light\") and on δέω (\"bind\") `[S: audit 4]`. **v1.2:** it is therefore nearly blind at 1:12–14. It also does not link ἀπολύτρωσις (\"redemption\") with λυτρόω (\"redeem\"), and it miscounts ἀφέστηκεν (\"has stood far off\", Isa 59:11, 14) as ἄφεσις (\"forgiveness\"). Do not quote ranks for that passage `[S: audit 5]`.")
