d.I("   The slave Onesimus is introduced with the same titles as Tychicus and Epaphras, \"faithful and beloved brother\", and \"one of you\" (4:9; 1:7; 4:7, 12) `[T]`.","   Onesimus is introduced with the same titles as Tychicus and Epaphras, \"faithful and beloved brother\", and \"one of you\" (4:9; 1:7; 4:7, 12) `[T]`. **v1.2: Colossians never calls him a slave.** That comes from Phlm 16, so say so when the two are joined; inside the letter δοῦλος (\"slave\") passes to Epaphras (4:12) `[T]` `[S: audit 5]`.")
d.R('   - εἴ γε is confident in Paul',"   - εἴ γε (\"if indeed\"; five uses in the SBLGNT) is confident at 2 Cor 5:3, Eph 3:2 and 4:21, but **not at Gal 3:4** (Pao, p. 109), and particles do not change the class of a condition (Robertson). So 1:23 is a real call to continue, spoken with confidence, *moderate–high* `[S: Logos 5]`. Wright: \"This promise, like most, has a condition\";")
